Done. Added to `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`:

- `public enum NoteParseError: Error, Equatable { case malformedFormat }`
- `public func parseNote(from text: String) throws -> Note`

Behavior: splits on the literal `\n---\n` separator; if it doesn't yield exactly 4 parts it throws `NoteParseError.malformedFormat`. Field 3 (pinned flag) must be exactly `"1"` or `"0"` — anything else also throws rather than being guessed. Body is passed to the existing `extractTags(from:)` for tags; missing fields aren't defaulted, they cause a malformed error.

